course: dictionary
lesson: 12573
title: Diminish: getting smaller
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To diminish means to become smaller, less or weaker. You use it when something shrinks, fades or gets quieter. «The noise diminished as the train went into the tunnel.» The noise did not stop at once. It got quieter and quieter, so diminished means got less.
explain: You can also diminish something on purpose: to make it smaller or less important. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning fits. The clues are the words that tell you what is changing.
explain: Diminish is a formal word, found often in reading and science. In everyday speech, people say go down, shrink or fade. «Our water supply diminished day by day.» Try the swap: «Our water supply went down day by day» still makes sense, so diminished means went down.
fact: Diminish means to become smaller, less or weaker.
fact: To diminish something means to make it smaller or less important.
fact: In maths, a diminishing amount gets smaller each time.
fact: Diminishing returns means each extra effort brings a smaller gain than the one before.
exercise: «The noise diminished as the train went into the tunnel.» What does diminished mean? | Got louder | Turned into music | *Got quieter | Changed colour
exercise: «Our water supply diminished day by day.» Which everyday words could you swap in for diminished? | jumped | *went down | went up | sang
exercise: What does it mean to diminish something? | To ask someone for help | To paint it bright red | *To make it smaller or less important | To make it bigger
test: «Her confidence diminished after the loss.» What does diminished suggest? | Was lost for ever | Became bigger and braver | *Got weaker | Stayed exactly the same
test: Which everyday word is a simpler match for diminish? | bounce | soar | shout | *shrink
exam: «The sun's warmth diminished as evening came.» What is the best meaning of diminished here? | Turned into a cloud | Became brighter and hotter | Stayed exactly the same | *Became weaker and less
